{"seq":16,"trial_id":"matrix-mu-2026-11/qm-pi-opus-none-mu-v03-dev/sy-03-marrow-fieldworks-ticket-numbers/r2","wall_ts":"2026-11-05T08:01:38.906Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-16T09:00:00-05:00","args_digest":"2efc519cdb02735e6ee1a89346295e4f0135996c2c64b381307323fedb95a459","actor":"assistant","via":"slack","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"DMATRIX0001","text":"Here are the Marrow Fieldworks ticket numbers I found:\n\n1. **#4409**, from Moss's note \"Central handoffs next week\" (2 Jan 2026). It's a recurring timeout on the Gatehouse Check-In report at the Salina North yard (Bay 4 and the west grain-bin apron, during the 06:00 flatbed intake). Hollis flagged it before the 5 Jan handoff.\n2. **#4412**, from the same Moss note. It's a driver SMS prompt glitch when staging combine trailers on unpaved overflow lots.\n3. **PD-5302**, from #central-random. Hollis posted it on Oct 14 as a follow-up from this week and said no action was needed. This is the only Marrow Fieldworks ticket in this week's chat.\n\n**One I'm not sure about:** On Oct 13 in #central-random, Tobias said he logged **#8841** on \"Tobias's dealer account.\" It's about West yard Door 2 double-booking when flatbeds check in early. Moss's January note says Marrow Fieldworks was your dealer account and changed hands on 5 Jan, but nothing I can see says it went to Tobias. So #8841 might be a Marrow Fieldworks ticket, but I can't confirm that. Tobias could tell you.\n\n**Left out on purpose:** FR-882 (custom pallet-jack icons) and PD-4821 (the Eastbank door import) are for Marrow Agrisupply, which is a different account. The rest of Moss's notes don't mention Marrow Fieldworks."},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"DMATRIX0001","ts":"1792159200.000127"}}
